      {
        "id": 17,
        "type": "Note",
        "title": "How to use this workflow",
        "pos": [
          1360,
          1020
        ],
        "size": [
          910,
          300
        ],
        "flags": {},
        "order": 4,
        "mode": 0,
        "inputs": [],
        "outputs": [],
        "properties": {
          "Node name for S&R": "Note"
        },
        "widgets_values": [
          "KREA-ONLY REBALANCE. Raw BF16, required full Identity Edit v1.2, 20 steps, CFG 3, Euler/simple. The original image-grounded encoders stay in place. Both positive and negative conditioning pass through ConditioningKrea2Rebalance before the sampler. It uses the pack's 12-layer weights with global multiplier 1.0 instead of its 4.0 default. This is an unbenchmarked starting recipe, not a promise of better likeness. No eight-step Rebalance schedule is used. Keep scene first and subject second in the two-image graph. Identity Edit stays at strength 1.0; optional LoRAs stay off. Keep output at 1 MP for the first comparison. Do not change the reference-to-latent connections. Review facial proportions, not only sharpness."
        ]
      },
